 adds $x_1$ to the first positive order","It ignores $x_1$, as the property needs $x_1=0$","It subtracts $x_1$ from the last demand $D_n$","It nets $x_1$ off $D_1,D_2,\\dots$ until used up"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"7fbe7e050dc8574b276aa523","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_zero_inventory_ordering_property_2c0517a6_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"A dynamic lot-size problem has demands $D=(25,15,30,20)$, $x_1=0$, setup cost 50 per order and holding cost 1 per unit of end-of-period stock $x_{i+1}$; the constant unit price is left out. What is the setup plus holding cost of the plan $y=(40,0,50,0)$?","options":["100","135","225","170"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"bfd5622d77dd4aefa6f81061","time_limit":30,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"no_diagnostic_value"},{"id":"year_1_1a_or_modelling_zero_inventory_ordering_property_2c0517a6_020","difficulty":"challenge","question_type":"application","question":"A dynamic lot-size problem has initial stock $x_1=25$, demands $D=(10,30,20,30)$, setup cost 40 per order and holding cost 1 per unit of end stock $x_{i+1}$; the constant unit price is left out. The initial stock is first netted off the demands period by period, and the zero-inventory ordering property is then applied to the net demands. Which of these order plans is optimal?","options":["(0, 15, 50, 0)","(0, 65, 0, 0)","(0, 35, 0, 30)","(0, 15, 20, 30)"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"164f6f789ce6475b1669def4","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-10-27T08:58:47.943104+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"}]}}